//File:    compilers.jtext
//Date:    2026-10-30
//Purpose: The compiler registry (v001): every toolchain jac313 builds with and, per OS family, how
//         to activate it and whether it is required. Read by jac313_test_cli (settings.cpp) and,
//         before anything is built, by bsir.sh (Setup/jtext_table.sh).
//
// toolchains: one row per toolchain, in the order they are sensed.
//   label        drives the build dir and the results label (gcc15, gcc16, clang)
//   kind         gcc | clang
//   version      --version MAJOR to match (terminology-independent: a bare `g++`
//                reporting this major satisfies the toolchain)
//   min_version  when not 0, accept MAJOR >= this; 0 = exact match on `version`
//   build_dir    out-of-source build tree for this toolchain
//   flag         selector for --compiler <flag> (the CLI's own choices are --gcc / --clang)
//   cc_names     compiler invocation names tried in order (space list)
//   scan_deps    (clang only) clang-scan-deps names to try for module builds (space list;
//                '' = none)
//
// toolchain_os: one row per OS family per activation, in order.
//   os              OS family: rhel | fedora | linuxmint (Setup's sensed os_family)
//   toolchain       a label in toolchains
//   required        true = REQUIRED on this OS family for a READY verdict (FileCheckList.txt);
//                   false = optional there (informational only)
//   activation_seq  the order the activations are tried in, 1 first
//   activation      command template; {CMD} is replaced with the probe command. Each is run
//                   via /bin/sh -c, so shell syntax is allowed. The FIRST (activation x
//                   cc_name) whose `cc --version` reports the right major wins.
//   A host whose OS family has no rows here tries every activation listed, in order, and
//   no toolchain is required on it.
//
// toolchain_min_os: an OS family's own minimum for a toolchain, replacing its min_version there.
//   Each OS has its own limit of the compilers its repositories offer, so a compiler change is
//   made for one OS family here, never for all of them in toolchains.
//   os           OS family: rhel | fedora | linuxmint
//   toolchain    a label in toolchains
//   min_version  this OS family's minimum MAJOR (0 = exact match on the toolchain's version)
//
// How activation generalizes: every mechanism (plain PATH binary, RHEL 10
// `gcc-toolset-NN-env`, RHEL 9 `scl enable`, a sourced enable-script, a future
// Fedora `module load`, Nix, conda, ...) just produces an environment in which the
// compiler is reachable. The tool captures that environment and applies it to every
// child process (configure, build, ctest, and each matrix test binary). To support a
// new platform, add its toolchain_os rows here: no code change.
//
// gcc15: RHEL-family via gcc-toolset-15, Linux Mint via the ubuntu-toolchain-r PPA.
//   Fedora does not require it: Fedora 44+ ships gcc 16 as its system compiler (see gcc16).
// gcc16: Fedora 44+ ships gcc 16 as the system compiler. jac313 compiles clean with it;
//   this entry runs + labels it accurately as gcc16 (never mislabeled gcc15).
// clang: the label stays "clang" (matches committed results paths); build_dir is build-clang
//   (no version in it: the version differs by OS). Required on all supported platforms.
//   Minimum 20; Linux Mint 21 (toolchain_min_os: bsir.sh installs clang-21 from apt.llvm.org).
//
// Formatter ^~ on the data rows (splice ^, comment ~): the activations hold |, ' and &&,
// and bsir.sh reads this file with POSIX awk before anything is built. Keep one row per
// line and no comments on data rows.
//
=== jText File ===
